        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بیٹھنا (baiṭhnā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from upaviśati, \"sits down\" (CDIAL 2245). The -ṭh- goes back to its past form upaviṣṭa, \"seated\"."
            }
          ]
        },
